{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"reasoning","text":"**Rewriting migration sorting logic**\n\nI’m updating the get_pending_migrations function to sort and compare migration versions numerically by converting version strings to integers. This fixes issues where string comparison caused \"10\" to sort before \"2\". I’m focusing only on lines 36-55 with minimal changes since audit logging can’t be added here due to import constraints."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_13","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"code\": \"    def get_pending_migrations(self) -> list[dict[str, Any]]:\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"Return migrations not yet applied, sorted by version.\\n\\n        BUG_48: versions are compared as *strings* so lexicographic\\n        ordering causes \\\"10\\\" to sort before \\\"2\\\" and pending detection\\n        incorrectly skips higher single-digit versions.\\n        \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n        version_key = lambda migration: int(migration[\\\"version\\\"])\\n\\n        if not self.applied_versions:\\n            return sorted(self.available_migrations, key=version_key)\\n\\n        max_applied = max(int(v) for v in self.applied_versions)\\n        pending = [\\n            migration\\n            for migration in self.available_migrations\\n            if int(migration[\\\"version\\\"]) > max_applied\\n        ]\\n        return sorted(pending, key=version_key)\\n\", \"comments\": \"Normalize versions to ints before comparing so pending migrations are ordered numerically.\"}"}}
